From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:43:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rometadata: metadata writer: IMetaDataEmit, IMetaDataEmit2,
 IMetaDataAssemblyEmit (3319)

DECISIONS-2 NET-META. DefineScope now returns a new scope, and OpenScope[OnMemory]
with ofWrite edits an existing one. The scope implements IMetaDataEmit/Emit2 (type,
nested type, method, field, parameter, property, event, member/type/module/assembly
references, type and method specs, generic parameters, constants, class layout,
field marshalling, permission sets and security attribute sets, platform invoke
maps, custom attributes, user strings, import of types/members and signature
translation from another scope) and IMetaDataAssemblyEmit, and keeps the
import interfaces: the reader sees the live state of the edit.

Tokens stay valid while a scope is edited: rows are never moved, the members of a
type are linked through pointer tables (the reader now understands FieldPtr,
MethodPtr, ParamPtr, EventPtr and PropertyPtr). Save, SaveToStream and
SaveToMemory write the standard layout (members of a type adjacent, sorted
tables sorted, no pointer tables) and tell the IMapToken handler about every
token that changed. Merge and edit-and-continue are not implemented.

